&gt;&gt;&gt; Optimal	Durability, Production
&gt;&gt; Suitable	Firefighters Gear/Armor
X Inadvisable 	Hospitals

Tools Recommended: Tree-cutting (highest), Cooking tools

Originally developed as military hardware, polymimetic alloy is programmable matter which is able to change states between liquid and solid. This allows it to be quickly formed and can maintain a rigid or flexible shape, suitible for everything from clothes, weapons, buildings, and armor. Because it can reform when damaged, it has unmatched longevity as a material. And because of this, armor made of it can be equipped almost instantly.</description>
